Subject: [PATCH] Do not repeat the export macro on the QoS default definitions

A namespace-scope `const` definition has internal linkage, and GCC refuses to
dllexport an internal-linkage symbol:

  error: external linkage required for symbol
      'eprosima::fastdds::dds::PUBLISHER_QOS_DEFAULT'
      because of 'dllexport' attribute

The headers already declare these objects `FASTDDS_EXPORTED_API extern const`,
which is what gives them external linkage and their export. Repeating the macro
on the definition adds nothing and makes GCC re-check the linkage at a point
where it is not yet external. MSVC does not object, which is why upstream CI
does not see this.

Note that upstream is already inconsistent here: the other five QoS defaults --
PARTICIPANT_FACTORY, PARTICIPANT, DATAWRITER, DATAREADER and TOPIC -- omit the
macro on their definitions and compile fine. This makes PUBLISHER and SUBSCRIBER
match them.

Adding `extern` instead would NOT work: `extern const T NAME;` with no
initialiser is a declaration, not a definition, and the symbol would go missing
at link time.
---
--- a/src/cpp/fastdds/publisher/qos/PublisherQos.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/fastdds/publisher/qos/PublisherQos.cpp
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 namespace fastdds {
 namespace dds {
 
-FASTDDS_EXPORTED_API const PublisherQos PUBLISHER_QOS_DEFAULT;
+const PublisherQos PUBLISHER_QOS_DEFAULT;
 
 
 } /* namespace dds */
--- a/src/cpp/fastdds/subscriber/qos/SubscriberQos.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/fastdds/subscriber/qos/SubscriberQos.cpp
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 namespace fastdds {
 namespace dds {
 
-FASTDDS_EXPORTED_API const SubscriberQos SUBSCRIBER_QOS_DEFAULT;
+const SubscriberQos SUBSCRIBER_QOS_DEFAULT;
 
 } /* namespace dds */
 } /* namespace fastdds */
